+\tif (r_return != nullptr) {\n+\t\tmemnew_placement(r_return, Variant(ret));\n+\t}","path":"core/extension/gdextension_interface.cpp","commit_id":"67a1c8f76991eeceb377e1a30cc0a478b40fb78a","original_commit_id":"67a1c8f76991eeceb377e1a30cc0a478b40fb78a","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Won't this mean that `Variant` is constructed twice now? Once via the default constructor by `Variant ret;` and then once again by `memnew_placement()`?\r\n\r\nTo avoid it, I think we'd need something like (untested):\r\n\r\n\r\n```suggestion\r\n\tVariant *ret = reinterpret_cast<Variant *>(r_return);\r\n\tif (ret == nullptr) {\r\n\t\tret = (Variant *)alloca(sizeof(Variant));\r\n\t}\r\n\tmemnew_placement(r_return, Variant)\r\n\tself->callp(method, args, p_argcount, *ret, error);\r\n```\r\n\r\nNot the prettiest code :-)\r\n\r\nBut it looks like all the other changes below also have an extra `Variant` construction and would need something like this to avoid it","created_at":"2026-02-05T16:26:11Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T16:36:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115859#discussion_r2770054569","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115859","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2770054569"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115859#discussion_r2770054569"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115859"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2770054569/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":334,"original_start_line":334,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":338,"original_line":338,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":11,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2808891625","pull_request_review_id":3804092517,"id":2808891625,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6nbEjp","diff_hunk":"@@ -1333,7 +1337,10 @@ static void gdextension_object_method_bind_call(GDExtensionMethodBindPtr p_metho\n \tconst Variant **args = (const Variant **)p_args;\n \tCallable::CallError error;\n \n-\tmemnew_placement(r_return, Variant(mb->call(o, args, p_arg_count, error)));\n+\tVariant ret = mb->call(o, args, p_arg_count, error);","path":"core/extension/gdextension_interface.cpp","commit_id":"67a1c8f76991eeceb377e1a30cc0a478b40fb78a","original_commit_id":"67a1c8f76991eeceb377e1a30cc0a478b40fb78a","user":{"login":"touilleMan","id":3187637,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODc2Mzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3187637?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan","html_url":"https://github.com/touilleMan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"do you know if doing \n```c++\n\tif (r_return != nullptr) {\n\t\tmemnew_placement(r_return, Variant(mb->call(o, args, p_arg_count, error)));\n\t} else {\n\t\tmb->call(o, args, p_arg_count, error);\n    }\n```\n\nis more performant ?","created_at":"2026-02-15T09:22:28Z","updated_at":"2026-02-15T09:46:44Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115859#discussion_r2808891625","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115859","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2808891625"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115859#discussion_r2808891625"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115859"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2808891625/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1340,"original_line":1340,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":35,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2808939256","pull_request_review_id":3804092517,"id":2808939256,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6nbQL4","diff_hunk":"@@ -331,9 +331,11 @@ static void gdextension_variant_call(GDExtensionVariantPtr p_self, GDExtensionCo\n \tconst StringName method = *reinterpret_cast<const StringName *>(p_method);\n \tconst Variant **args = (const Variant **)p_args;\n \tCallable::CallError error;\n-\tmemnew_placement(r_return, Variant);\n-\tVariant *ret = reinterpret_cast<Variant *>(r_return);\n-\tself->callp(method, args, p_argcount, *ret, error);\n+\tVariant ret;\n+\tself->callp(method, args, p_argcount, ret, error);\n+\tif (r_return != nullptr) {\n+\t\tmemnew_placement(r_return, Variant(ret));\n+\t}","path":"core/extension/gdextension_interface.cpp","commit_id":"67a1c8f76991eeceb377e1a30cc0a478b40fb78a","original_commit_id":"67a1c8f76991eeceb377e1a30cc0a478b40fb78a","user":{"login":"touilleMan","id":3187637,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODc2Mzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3187637?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan","html_url":"https://github.com/touilleMan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/touilleMan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> Won't this mean that Variant is constructed twice now?\n\nI would go even further and say this Variant is constructed three times !\n\n- Once in `Variant ret`\n- Once in `memnew_placement(r_return, Variant(ret));`\n- An once within `callp` since this functions takes the ret parameter as a reference (i.e. `Variant &ret` ). So `ret`'s destructor is first called, then the actual return value is copied into it.\n\nThat's outside of the scope of this PR, but have we considered replacing the `Variant &ret` by a `Variant *r_uninitialized_ret` and then do the `memnew_placement(r_uninitialized_ret, ...)` within `callp` ?\n\nIn theory this would remove all the extra variant initialization (but in practice the compiler might already be smart enough when attempting to inline callp inside the caller, and figure out the intermediary variants can be omitted...)\n","created_at":"2026-02-15T09:46:07Z","updated_at":"2026-02-15T09:46:44Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115859#discussion_r2808939256","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115859","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2808939256"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115859#discussion_r2808939256"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115859"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2808939256/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":334,"original_start_line":334,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":338,"original_line":338,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2770054569,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":11,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"}]